# Secrets. This repo is public and `git add -A` is the normal way to commit here, so an
# env file created for a one-off command (seeding KV, testing the help form) would
# otherwise be swept in with everything else. KV_REST_API_TOKEN, RESEND_API_KEY,
# PATREON_CLIENT_SECRET, GEMINI_API_KEY and SESSION_SECRET all live in the Vercel
# dashboard — nothing but a local convenience copy should ever match these lines.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Vercel CLI link state (project and org ids, and a local env cache).
.vercel

# Never needed: the site is buildless and ships no dependencies.
node_modules/

# OS and editor droppings.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
